{"Channel": {"name": "bug-georgebrown-SearchFlow", "channelID": "ch-hflow-8b2bf1"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_e01a396c", "timestamp": "2026-08-20T04:54:00", "text": "Hi team, the bug titled 'Search Input Field Locks During Query Execution' has been resolved. You can check the approved PR here: https://github.com/salesforce/SearchFlow/pull/45.", "utterranceID": "20260819-0-10b41"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260819-0-10b41"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-georgebrown-SearchFlow", "channelID": "ch-hflow-8b2bf1"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_e01a396c", "timestamp": "2026-08-20T04:55:00", "text": "The root cause was that the input field was being disabled during search execution to prevent changes, but it wasn't being re-enabled until the search completed.", "utterranceID": "20260819-1-a0614"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260819-1-a0614"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-georgebrown-SearchFlow", "channelID": "ch-hflow-8b2bf1"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_e01a396c", "timestamp": "2026-08-20T05:00:00", "text": "To fix this, I modified the event listener to re-enable the input field as soon as the search execution starts, allowing users to modify or cancel the query if needed. This ensures the field is only locked when absolutely necessary.", "utterranceID": "20260819-2-deae5"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260819-2-deae5"}
